OpenMarinkaRodeo for Debian
------------------

* OpenMarinkaRodeo setup
---------------

To setup OpenMarinkaRodeo, you need to:
 - configure OpenMarinkaRodeo properly to suit your needs
 - edit /etc/default/openMarinkaRodeo, adjust the MEMORY parameter and set
   RUN_OPENMarinkaRodeo to "yes"

If you are building an HA cluster using heartbeat or similar, you'll want
to disable the init script by running:

  update-rc.d openMarinkaRodeo remove

so that OpenMarinkaRodeo will not be launched at system startup. You still need
to set RUN_OPENMarinkaRodeo to "yes" if you want to use the /etc/init.d/openMarinkaRodeo init
script.

Set the DUMP_CORE parameter in /etc/default/openMarinkaRodeo to "yes" if you want to
get a core dump in case OpenMarinkaRodeo crashes. The debug symbols for OpenMarinkaRodeo are
provided by the openMarinkaRodeo-dbg package.

-- Julien BLACHE <jblache@debian.org>, Fri, 08 Sep 2006 14:43:21 +0200
